# counter harness. One force call is one SpecPotentialModel evaluation of the problem potential.
# FIRE is the ASE flavor. Gradient descent uses pos_lr. The cell stays fixed.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# LJ38 removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6). The noise-aware stop supplies that force_norm when sigma is positive.
# Morse bulk uses the full Hessian. A curvature below -1e-6 is negative.
# Energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied.
# A returned geometry is one cluster inside the problem bound distance. A dissociated geometry is divergence.
# Default profile. Gradient descent uses the constructor pos_lr 0.01. The step is that rate times the force, and this optimizer has no displacement cap. SpecPotentialModel evaluates the problem potential. Opening forces on these Lennard-Jones starts are large enough that this step can leave the cutoff.
